<title>USA: CBS wins weekly prime time ratings battle.</title>
<headline>CBS wins weekly prime time ratings battle.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westinghouse Electric Co unit CBS Inc took the top ratings spot attracting evening-hours audiences during the week ended October 6 of the 1996-97 U.S. television season, Neilsen Media Research said on Tuesday. </p>
<p>According to Neilsen Media Research, General Electric Co unit NBC took second place and the ABC network owned by Walt Disney Co was third in the number of homes tuned to its evening-hours programs.</p>
<p>The FOX network owned by News Corp Ltd was fourth.</p>
</text>
